Subtask 1.3: Add Users to Groups
Learn how to add individual users and multiple users to groups using various methods.

Step 1: Add single users to groups

# Add John Smith to IT department
ipa group-add-member it-department --users=jsmith

# Add Mary Jones to HR department
ipa group-add-member hr-department --users=mjones

# Add Bob Wilson to Finance department
ipa group-add-member finance-department --users=bwilson
Step 2: Add multiple users to a single group

# Add multiple users to marketing department
ipa group-add-member marketing-department --users=slee,jsmith
Step 3: Verify group memberships

# Check IT department membership
ipa group-show it-department

# Check marketing department membership
ipa group-show marketing-department
Subtask 1.4: Understanding Group Membership Output
Step 1: Analyze group membership information

# Display detailed group information
ipa group-show it-department --all
The output will show:

Member users: Direct user members
Member groups: Nested group members (if any)
Indirect members: Users who are members through nested groups
