Best Practices for Group Management
1. Naming Conventions
Use descriptive, consistent naming patterns
Include department or function prefixes
Use lowercase with hyphens for readability
2. Group Hierarchy Design
Keep nesting levels reasonable (typically 2-3 levels maximum)
Design hierarchies that match organizational structure
Document group purposes and relationships
3. Membership Management
Regularly audit group memberships
Use automation for large-scale changes
Implement approval processes for sensitive groups
4. Performance Considerations
Monitor SSSD performance with large nested groups
Consider group size limits for optimal performance
Use caching strategies appropriately
