Why This Matters
Group membership management and nested groups are fundamental to enterprise identity management because they:

Simplify Access Control: Instead of managing individual user permissions, you can assign permissions to groups
Reflect Organizational Structure: Nested groups mirror real company hierarchies and reporting relationships
Reduce Administrative Overhead: Changes to group membership automatically propagate permissions
Enable Role-Based Access: Users can have multiple roles through different group memberships
Support Compliance: Proper group management helps meet audit and compliance requirements
